From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 05:01:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuilt: net proceeds and the HOA hub; every page has six or
 more referring pages

- /sell/net-proceeds/ leads with what a seller here pays and keeps, worked on a real price, with the
  costs set in state law, deed stamps, the payoff, the HOA letter and the tax hold-back.
- /hoa/ gives typical monthly fees by kind of home (condo, oceanfront tower, townhouse, house) and
  what each covers, from listings counted in aggregate; /hoa/hoa-vs-poa/ now prints the same figures
  and links the hub for fees.
- Owner, 2026-11-09: "make sure every page has referring pages". 47 thinly linked pages raised to
  six or more pages linking from their text, on existing words where possible.
- /buyers/retirees/: McLeod Carolina Forest opened to patients in October 2026.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
