 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the cheapest neighborhood to buy a home near Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Of the neighborhoods within about 20 minutes of the beach where at least 10 homes sold in the past year, Parkview had the lowest prices. Its older townhomes usually sold for about $190,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can you buy a new house near Myrtle Beach for less?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In Birchwood, off SC 905 near Longs, new Lennar houses usually sold for about $225,000 in the past year. In Indigo Grove, off SC 90, they usually sold for about $245,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to buy in Conway than in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A home that resold in Conway in the past year usually went for about $265,000. In the city of Myrtle Beach, a home usually went for about $420,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you have to be a first-time buyer to get down-payment help?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, not in Horry or Georgetown County. Palmetto Home Advantage, an SC Housing down-payment program, is open to repeat buyers too. Our page on down-payment help programs covers it and the Homebuyer Program."}}]}</script>
