 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I apply for the 4 percent rate in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Online, on the county's Online Services page, under Legal Residence Application. If the county asks for a missing paper, you can send it by mail, fax or email, or bring it to the Assessor's Office. The office's phone number is 843-915-5040."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How far back can I get a refund of the 6 percent tax on my home?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"If you qualified for the 4 percent rate and paid at 6 percent, you can claim the extra tax back from the county assessor. Under state law, you have two years from the day you paid that bill, and a county council may allow refunds of the county's own share for more past years."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a condo's HOA fee show whether it has saved enough for repairs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. In our count of condos for sale here, the middle HOA fee is about $640 a month, and about $690 in buildings built in 1986 or earlier. Older buildings do not charge much more, so the fee alone does not show what a building has saved for its age."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I change jobs while buying a house in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Wait until after closing if you can. On a loan that follows Fannie Mae's rules, the lender checks again that you still have your job no more than 10 business days before closing, or 15 in some cases. A loan officer at our preferred lender can tell you what your loan will need."}}]}</script>
