 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-maryland/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is South Carolina cheaper than Maryland?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On tax, yes for most households, and the county income tax is the reason. Every Maryland county and Baltimore City charges one on top of the state rate, and most sit at 3.20 percent. South Carolina has no local income tax anywhere. Property tax and a typical house both cost less here too."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Maryland have a local income tax?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every county and Baltimore City levies one on top of the state rate. On the Comptroller’s 2025 chart the rates run from 2.65 percent to 3.30 percent, with most counties at 3.20 percent. Two changed for 2026: Allegany rose to 3.20 percent and Kent to 3.30 percent. South Carolina charges none."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Maryland tax my retirement income?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Social Security is not taxed in Maryland. Other pension and retirement income is taxed, with a pension exclusion for taxpayers who are 65 or older or totally disabled: $39,500 for tax year 2024 and $41,200 for tax year 2025, indexed each year. Military retirees at least 55 may subtract up to $20,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Maryland estate and inheritance tax?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Maryland is the only state with both. The estate tax applies above a $5 million exemption at rates up to 16 percent, and a separate inheritance tax applies to property passing to non-lineal heirs. Direct lineal heirs are exempt from the inheritance tax. South Carolina has neither."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will I pay a new tax on my car in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, and for most movers it is the surprise. South Carolina taxes every vehicle on its value each year, and the county bill must be paid before the plate renews. A car titled elsewhere also pays a one-time $250 fee at first registration, and you have 45 days from the move to register."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a house cost in Myrtle Beach compared with Maryland?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A typical home here costs about $342,000, against a Maryland statewide average of about $433,000 on the same July 2026 Zillow measure. Your own county can sit far from that average, so compare your city with here on our cost of living calculator."}}]}</script>
