 bill or approved application for service, a bank statement, an insurance bill, a pay stub, or the Postal Service change-of-address confirmation. One proof gets you a standard license; two get you a REAL ID at the same price.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">Your out-of-state driver&#39;s license.</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">You surrender it.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">The name of an auto insurer licensed in South Carolina.</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">Switch your policy before the DMV visit; the county wants it too.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">For each vehicle</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">the current out-of-state registration or title, and the lienholder&#39;s name if there is a loan.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">If married</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">your spouse&#39;s license and registration will be needed for the property tax application later, even if the house is in one name.</span></div></div></div></section>
+<section id="papers" style="background:var(--ivory-2);scroll-margin-top:120px"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Before the truck leaves</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">What to bring, because the DMV will ask for it</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every step below asks for the same short stack of paper. Pack it in the car, not the moving truck. If you have children, school registration has its own list, on our page on <a href="/buyers/relocating/schools/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">school zones and registration</a>.</p><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);max-width:760px;margin-top:1.4rem"><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">Proof of who you are</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">a certified birth certificate or an unexpired U.S. passport.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">Your Social Security number.</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">The DMV checks it electronically; the card itself is not required, but the number is.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">Two proofs of your new South Carolina address, from two different organizations, dated within nine months</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">: a lease or closing statement, a utility bill or approved application for service, a bank statement, an insurance bill, a pay stub, or the Postal Service change-of-address confirmation. One proof gets you a standard license; two get you a REAL ID at the same price.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">Your out-of-state driver&#39;s license.</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">You surrender it.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">The name of an auto insurer licensed in South Carolina.</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">Switch your policy before the DMV visit; the county wants it too.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">For each vehicle</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">the current out-of-state registration or title, and the lienholder&#39;s name if there is a loan.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">If married</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">your spouse&#39;s license and registration will be needed for the property tax application later, even if the house is in one name.</span></div></div></div></section>
 
 <section id="dmv" style="background:var(--ivory);scroll-margin-top:120px"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Week one</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Insurance, then the county, then the DMV: the order matters</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina charges an annual property tax on cars, paid a year in advance to the county, and the DMV will not register a vehicle until it is paid. The sequence is fixed. Get South Carolina auto insurance. Take each vehicle&#39;s registration or title and proof of your Horry County address to the county Auditor, who writes the vehicle tax notice. Pay it at the county Treasurer. Take the paid receipt to the DMV.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Myrtle Beach the county Auditor and Treasurer are at 1201 21st Avenue North and the DMV branch is at 1200 21st Avenue North, across the street. In Little River the county office and the DMV share 107 Highway 57 North. Conway has the county offices at 1301 Second Avenue and the DMV at 4103 Highway 701 North. Offices run weekdays; the DMV opens at 8:30 and at 9:30 on Wednesdays. There is no DMV branch in Surfside, Socastee, or Carolina Forest.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.4rem 0 .5rem">What each vehicle costs</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At the DMV: a one-time $250 infrastructure maintenance fee, a $15 title fee, and $40 for a plate and registration that lasts two years. That is $305 per standard passenger vehicle. The $250 fee is South Carolina&#39;s version of vehicle sales tax, and you pay it once, on arrival, in place of tax on a car you already own. Owners 65 and older pay $36 for the plate instead of $40.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At the county: the vehicle tax, which New York, New Jersey, Pennsylvania and Ohio do not charge and which surprises almost everyone who arrives from them. It is not only cars: the county also bills boats and campers every year, so count them when you budget. Vehicles are assessed at 6 percent of value and then taxed at the local millage, and it comes due every year with the plate renewal. Horry County publishes a <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/tax-payer-services/vehicle-tax/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none" rel="noopener" target="_blank">vehicle tax estimator</a> on its vehicle tax page. A high-mileage discount exists, but only in the month the tax is due, so ask the Auditor about it at the counter.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.4rem 0 .5rem">The license itself</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px">Same visit if you brought the paperwork above. An eight-year license is $25. Expect a vision test; if your old license has been expired nine months or more, expect the knowledge and road tests too. Military members and students living here temporarily can keep their home-state license.</p><div style="background:var(--ivory);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:6px;padding:1.2rem 1.3rem;margin-top:1.8rem;max-width:720px;display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between"><p style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;font-weight:600">Buying before you move? We can time the closing around these dates.</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass" href="#lead-form">Ask about my move</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></div></section>
 
