 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it better to live in Myrtle Beach or North Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A typical house costs about the same in both: $535,000 in Myrtle Beach and $565,000 in North Myrtle Beach. In North Myrtle Beach it is closer to the beach, but more often in the high-risk flood zone. Myrtle Beach is much closer to the airport, and most of its neighborhoods of houses are not zoned for nightly rentals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a Myrtle Beach address mean the house is in the city?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not always. Carolina Forest houses, and many in Socastee, have Myrtle Beach mailing addresses but are outside the city limits. They pay no city tax and get no city trash pickup. We check the city line for any address you send us."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where near Myrtle Beach are most houses someone's home all year?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In most of these places, about 3 in 4 houses or more are the owner's main home, taxed at the 4 percent rate. In North Myrtle Beach about half are, and in Surfside Beach fewer than half. The rest are taxed at the 6 percent rate for second homes and rentals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which town near Myrtle Beach has the least crime?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Chapter3 does not rate any town on crime or describe who lives anywhere. Fair housing law bars agents from steering buyers toward or away from an area. We give you the record of the house itself: its flood zone, its tax and the rules for its address."}}]}</script>
