 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach the fastest growing city in America?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, but it is close. The Myrtle Beach area, which is all of Horry County, grew the second fastest of any metro area from mid-2024 to mid-2025, behind Ocala, Florida. The City of Myrtle Beach itself has about 41,000 people."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are people leaving Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Some are. In the latest count, about 9,100 households left Horry County and about 15,000 arrived. Most who leave go nearby, to Georgetown or Charleston County in South Carolina or Brunswick County, North Carolina."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where do most people moving to Myrtle Beach come from?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About six in seven come from another state, most from the South and the Northeast. The single largest source is Georgetown County, SC. Outside South Carolina, the most come from Suffolk County on Long Island."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to live in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Homes and property tax usually cost less than in the out-of-state counties most movers come from. Home insurance costs more than in the rest of South Carolina, and local pay is lower."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is winter like in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Short and mild. A January day averages a high of about 56 degrees and a low of about 37, and snow averages about an inch a year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does South Carolina tax Social Security?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, South Carolina does not tax Social Security. Military retirement pay is not taxed either."}}]}</script>
