1.4"/><g transform="translate(11 305)"><g class="k"><text class="f">10 MILES</text></g></g><g transform="translate(343 21)"><g class="k"><path d="M0-12 5 2 0-1-5 2z" fill="#1c2028"/><text class="f" y="15" text-anchor="middle">N</text></g></g><g transform="translate(79.2 101.5)"><g class="k"><text class="T" x="0" y="3.7" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="0">CONWAY</tspan></text></g></g><g transform="translate(220 200)"><g class="k"><text class="o" x="0" y="5.1" text-anchor="middle">Atlantic Ocean</text></g></g><g transform="translate(198 137.7)"><g class="k"><path d="M-10.7 -8H10.7V1.2C10.7 6.4 4.8 8 0 9.6C-4.8 8 -10.7 6.4 -10.7 1.2z" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.1"/><text class="r" y="3.1" text-anchor="middle">17</text></g></g><g transform="translate(101.4 223.1)"><g class="k"><path d="M-21.5 -8H21.5V1.2C21.5 6.4 9.7 8 0 9.6C-9.7 8 -21.5 6.4 -21.5 1.2z" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.1"/><text class="r" y="3.1" text-anchor="middle">17<tspan class="q" dx="2">BYP</tspan></text></g></g><g transform="translate(103.8 125.8)"><g class="k"><path d="M-14.7 -8H14.7V1.2C14.7 6.4 6.6 8 0 9.6C-6.6 8 -14.7 6.4 -14.7 1.2z" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.1"/><text class="r" y="3.1" text-anchor="middle">501</text></g></g><g transform="translate(207.4 115.3)"><g class="k"><rect x="-10.7" y="-8" width="21.5" height="16" rx="3" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.1"/><text class="r" y="4" text-anchor="middle">31</text></g></g><g><g transform="translate(160.6 167)"><g class="k"><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><text class="ab" y="4.5" text-anchor="middle">1</text></g></g><g transform="translate(136.7 142.2)"><g class="k"><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><text class="ab" y="4.5" text-anchor="middle">2</text></g></g><g transform="translate(98.8 185.2)"><g class="k"><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><text class="ab" y="4.5" text-anchor="middle">3</text></g></g><g transform="translate(79.9 260.7)"><g class="k"><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><text class="ab" y="4.5" text-anchor="middle">4</text></g></g><g transform="translate(274.8 77.7)"><g class="k"><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><text class="ab" y="4.5" text-anchor="middle">5</text></g></g></g></svg><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.6rem">The City of Myrtle Beach and four places outside any city where many of the new homes are. The outlines are the Census Bureau's. Map data: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line; Horry County GIS.</figcaption></figure><ol class="c3w-key" role="list" aria-label="Map key"><li><b>1</b>City of Myrtle Beach, about 41,000 people</li><li><b>2</b>Carolina Forest, outside city limits</li><li><b>3</b>Socastee, outside city limits</li><li><b>4</b>Murrells Inlet, outside city limits</li><li><b>5</b>Little River, outside city limits</li></ol></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Outside city limits is not far from the sand. With no traffic, the beach is about 10 minutes from the middle house in Murrells Inlet, 13 in Socastee, 14 in Little River and 18 in Carolina Forest.</p><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-why-myrtle-beach/woods-cleared-for-new-streets-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-why-myrtle-beach/woods-cleared-for-new-streets-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/buyers-relocating-why-myrtle-beach/woods-cleared-for-new-streets-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of two new subdivisions being cut out of pine woods: a paved street loop around a pond with empty lots, and more streets being graded across the road" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo, 2023. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo, 2023</a></span></div><figcaption>Woods cleared for new streets and house lots outside the city limits, between Conway and North Myrtle Beach.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Summer traffic is lighter than most movers expect. In our team's experience, rush hour adds 5 to 10 minutes, and <a href="/buyers/relocating/getting-around/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">SC 31 or SC 22 avoids the many stop lights on US 17</a>. Our <a href="/buyers/relocating/which-town/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">which town page</a> compares the towns.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">New homes going up outside the city limits</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us your price and how far from the beach you want to live. We send you new homes for sale that fit.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send me new homes for sale</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="where-from"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Where from">Where are people moving to Myrtle Beach from?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About six in seven households that move to Horry County come from another state. The South sends the most, then the Northeast.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=row]{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;column-gap:.8rem;align-items:start}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .b{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .dot{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .f{display:block}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=cell]{justify-content:flex-end}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact c3-gchart-list"><div role="table" aria-label="Households that moved to Horry County in one year, by where they came from"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Households that moved to Horry County in one year, by where they came from</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Came from, note</span><span role="columnheader">households</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The South, outside South Carolina</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.833" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 5,900</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The Northeast</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.695" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 4,900</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Other South Carolina counties</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">most from Georgetown County</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.306" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 2,200</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The Midwest</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.167" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 1,200</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The West</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.136" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 1,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>IRS counts of households that changed county. The South includes North Carolina, Virginia, Maryland and Florida.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The single county that sends the most is Georgetown County, South Carolina, just to the south, with about 530 households in the latest count. Outside South Carolina, the most come from Suffolk County on Long Island, then Brunswick, Mecklenburg and Wake counties in North Carolina.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Few go back north. For every household that moved from Horry County to Ocean County, New Jersey, about five came from it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About six in ten Horry County residents were born in another state, against about one in four Americans. About 3 in 10 homes sold here in the last 12 months went to a buyer whose tax bill goes to another state or country.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We wrote a page for the move from each of the states most movers come from:</p><ul class="c3w-states" role="list"><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-new-york/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">New York</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-new-jersey/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">New Jersey</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-pennsylvania/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Pennsylvania</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-connecticut/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Connecticut</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-massachusetts/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Massachusetts</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-maryland/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Maryland</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-virginia/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Virginia</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-north-carolina/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">North Carolina</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-ohio/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Ohio</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-florida/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Florida</a></li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="what-your-house-buys"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What your house buys">What would my house buy in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In most of the out-of-state counties that send the most movers, a typical home is worth more than one here. Sell a typical Suffolk County home and buy a typical one here, and about $410,000 is left before moving costs, sale costs and any loan payoff.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From Ohio and the Pittsburgh area, the reverse is true: a typical home here costs more than one there. Pick your county to see the gap.</p><div class="c3-wbuys c3-calc-box" style="background:var(--navy);background-image:linear-gradient(160deg,rgba(42,48,64,.97),rgba(28,32,40,.98));border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14);border-radius:18px;padding:1.4rem 1.3rem 1.3rem;margin:1.6rem 0;max-width:620px;box-shadow:0 26px 60px -30px rgba(28,32,40,.6)"><p style="font-size:.85rem;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass-2);margin:0 0 .4rem;font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600">What your house buys here</p><label for="wbCounty" style="display:block;color:rgba(244,239,232,.92);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.4;margin:0 0 .45rem">The county you live in now</label><select id="wbCounty" onchange="c3Wb()" style="width:100%;max-width:100%;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.4);border-radius:10px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;padding:.65rem .7rem"><option value="852000">Nassau County, NY</option><option value="787000">Monmouth County, NJ</option><option value="756000">Fairfax County, VA</option><option value="730000">Suffolk County, NY</option><option value="551000">Ocean County, NJ</option><option value="505000">Dutchess County, NY</option><option value="471000">Wake County, NC</option><option value="468000">Orange County, NY</option><option value="455000">Maricopa County, AZ</option><option value="415000" selected>Mecklenburg County, NC</option><option value="404000">Brunswick County, NC</option><option value="358000">Baltimore County, MD</option><option value="292000">Franklin County (Columbus), OH</option><option value="237000">Allegheny County, PA</option><option value="228000">Cumberland County, NC</option><option value="219000">Cuyahoga County (Cleveland), OH</option><option value="198000">Columbus County, NC</option></select><div style="display:grid;gap:.55rem;margin-top:1.1rem"><div class="c3-wr"><span>A typical home there</span><strong id="wbThere">$415,000</strong></div><div class="c3-wr"><span>A typical home in Horry County</span><strong id="wbHere">$320,000</strong></div></div><div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.22);margin-top:1rem;padding-top:.9rem"><p id="wbSay" aria-live="polite" style="font-family:var(--sans);color:rgba(244,239,232,.92);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 .9rem;font-size:1.05rem">About $95,000 less here, before moving and sale costs.</p><a id="wbLink" class="c3-wblink" href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;max=415000">See houses for sale at or under $415,000</a></div></div><script>function c3Wb(){var s=document.getElementById("wbCounty");if(!s)return;var v=parseInt(s.value,10),here=320000;var m=function(n){return "$"+Math.round(n).toLocaleString("en-US")};var t=document.getElementById("wbThere"),y=document.getElementById("wbSay"),l=document.getElementById("wbLink");if(!t||!y||!l)return;t.textContent=m(v);var d=Math.round((v-here)/1000)*1000;y.textContent=d>0?"About "+m(d)+" less here, before moving and sale costs.":d<0?"About "+m(-d)+" more here than there.":"About the same as here.";l.href="/homes/map/?type=house&max="+v;l.textContent="See houses for sale at or under "+m(v)}document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",c3Wb);</script><style>main#main .c3-wbuys .c3-wr{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:1rem;font-family:var(--sans);color:rgba(244,239,232,.88);font-size:1rem}main#main .c3-wbuys .c3-wr strong{color:var(--brass-2);font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.5rem;line-height:1.1;white-space:nowrap}main#main .c3-wbuys .c3-wblink{display:inline-block;color:var(--brass-2);font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.2em;line-height:1.4;padding:.35rem 0}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">These are county figures, not a value for your house. We price the house you want here against nearby sales.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About half of the houses for sale here are priced at or under a typical Charlotte-area home's value.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=row]{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;column-gap:.8rem;align-items:start}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .b{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .dot{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .f{display:block}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=cell]{justify-content:flex-end}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact c3-gchart-list"><div role="table" aria-label="Houses for sale here at or under a typical home's value in each county"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Houses for sale here at or under a typical home's value in each county</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Typical home value in, price line</span><span role="columnheader">houses for sale</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Nassau County, NY</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">at or under $852,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.759" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 3,230</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Suffolk County, NY</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">at or under $730,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.718" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 3,050</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Mecklenburg County, NC</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">at or under $415,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.435" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 1,850</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Horry County, SC</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">at or under $320,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.235" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 1,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Houses only, not condos, out of about 3,700 houses for sale in Horry and Georgetown counties and nearby. We ran this count on November 3, 2026; ask us and we run it again for your price.</figcaption></figure><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">The houses your budget buys here</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us what you expect from your sale up north. We send you the houses for sale it buys, town by town.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send us your budget</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="jobs-and-pay"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Jobs and pay">Are there jobs in Myrtle Beach, and what does work pay?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, and the number of jobs grew faster than in the country. Pay is lower, though: the average job here pays about 64 cents for every dollar of the national average.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Jobs and pay in Horry County and the country</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col" class="n">More jobs, 2019 to 2025</th><th scope="col" class="n">Average pay a year</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Horry County</th><td class="n" data-label="More jobs, 2019 to 2025">About 9%</td><td class="n" data-label="Average pay a year">About $50,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">United States</th><td class="n" data-label="More jobs, 2019 to 2025">About 5%</td><td class="n" data-label="Average pay a year">About $79,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of our buyers who need work find it within a month or two, in fields from child protective services and stores to welding. That is our clients' experience, not a promise.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Many movers bring their work with them. About half of our clients who come from the northern states arrive with a remote job.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Business owners who move here tell us they cannot charge as much for their services as they did up north. Our <a href="/buyers/relocating/jobs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">jobs page</a> has more on work and pay here.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="taxes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Taxes and insurance">How much are taxes and insurance in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Property tax on a home you live in is low here, a fraction of the bill in most of the out-of-state counties movers come from.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=row]{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;column-gap:.8rem;align-items:start}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .b{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .dot{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .f{display:block}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=cell]{justify-content:flex-end}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact c3-gchart-list"><div role="table" aria-label="The typical yearly property tax bill on a home its owner lives in"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">The typical yearly property tax bill on a home its owner lives in</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">County</span><span role="columnheader">tax a year</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Suffolk County, NY</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.714" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$10,000 or more</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Nassau County, NY</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.714" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$10,000 or more</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Orange County, NY</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.607" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$8,494</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Ocean County, NJ</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.469" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$6,562</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Wake County, NC</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.233" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$3,260</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Mecklenburg County, NC</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.206" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$2,890</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Brunswick County, NC</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.135" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,890</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Horry County, SC</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.067" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$944</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Census Bureau, the middle bill paid by owners who live in their homes, averaged over five years. The Census table stops at $10,000.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The bills in the chart are what owners pay today. For a house you buy, budget from its price: about $1,470 a year on a $400,000 house you live in outside the city limits. It is about $4,820 if it is a second home or a rental.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Home insurance costs more than in the rest of the state</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Owners of a house in Horry County pay about $2,000 a year for home insurance at the middle, against about $1,400 in the rest of South Carolina.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Flood insurance depends on the street. Outside FEMA's high-risk flood zone, federal rules do not require it, and a policy usually costs about $550 a year. Inside it, your lender requires one, usually about $1,070.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Few houses in Carolina Forest, Conway, Myrtle Beach or Little River are in the high-risk zone: 5 percent or fewer. In Garden City, Surfside Beach and around Pawleys Island, about 3 in 10 are. We get you an insurance quote on a house before you make an offer.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">If you are retired</h3><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">South Carolina <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c006.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">does not tax Social Security</a>.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">From the year you turn 65, up to $10,000 a year of retirement income is deducted for each person. A second deduction brings the total to $15,000 a person against any income. Military retirement pay is not taxed at all.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">At 65, after a year living in South Carolina, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c037.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">you pay no property tax</a> on the first $50,000 of your home's value. For 2026 only, an owner who already qualified in 2025 gets $75,000.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">South Carolina <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c016.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">has no estate tax</a>.</li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The tax many movers do not expect</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina taxes vehicles every year. One of our team moved here from a village of about 400 in Ohio, and his first vehicle tax bill was $325.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each car first titled in another state also pays a <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t56c003.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">one-time $250 state fee</a> when you register it here. Owners on active duty in the military, and their spouses and dependents, do not pay it.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">The tax bill on one house, before you offer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Pick a house you like. We work out its property tax as your full-time home and as a second home.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us work out the tax</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="why-people-leave"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Who leaves, and why">Are people leaving Myrtle Beach, and why?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Some are, but fewer than arrive. In the latest count, about 9,100 households left Horry County and about 15,000 arrived. The top destinations for households that leave Horry County are nearby: Georgetown County, SC, Brunswick County, NC, and Charleston County, SC.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=row]{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;column-gap:.8rem;align-items:start}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .b{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .dot{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .f{display:block}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=cell]{justify-content:flex-end}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact c3-gchart-list"><div role="table" aria-label="Where the most households went when they left Horry County, in one year"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Where the most households went when they left Horry County, in one year</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Went to, note</span><span role="columnheader">households</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Georgetown County, SC</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">next door, to the south</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.799" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 490</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Brunswick County, NC</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">next door, to the north</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.368" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 220</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Charleston County, SC</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.367" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 220</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>IRS counts of households that changed county.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Those who leave reported less income: about $55,000 a household on average, against about $83,000 for those who arrived.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Making friends is harder than movers expect, because many people near the city core are tourists or a seasonal population that leaves. Our advice: buy outside the City of Myrtle Beach. Be a regular at places tourists do not go, such as gyms and clubs.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Summers are hot and humid: about 21 days a year reach 90 degrees. Hurricane season is June through November, and across the Atlantic most activity comes between mid-August and mid-October.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/buyers/relocating/hurricanes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">hurricane page</a> lists the storms that have hit this coast and what each one did.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="should-you-move"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Should you move?">Should you move to Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The move usually works for people who bring their money or their income with them. It is harder for people who need a local salary like the one they had up north. The rest is on our page on <a href="/buyers/relocating/pros-and-cons/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the honest pros and cons of living here year-round</a>.</p><ul class="c3-rc" role="list"><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span>If your home is worth more than a typical one here</span></p><p class="a">Selling it can pay for a home here with money left over, before costs. The tool above shows the gap for your county.</p></li><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span>If you live on a pension, Social Security or a remote job</span></p><p class="a">Lower local pay matters less to you, and the retiree tax breaks in the taxes section apply to you.</p></li><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span><span>If you need a local job</span></p><p class="a">Plan on lower pay than up north, and apply for jobs on your house-hunting visit. One of our clients applied for a child protective services job on a visit and was hired a month later.</p></li><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span><span>If you want to be outside all winter</span></p><p class="a">A day that stays below freezing from morning to night comes about once in three years. In our team's experience, the Boardwalk stays open all winter.</p></li><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span>If you want big-city night life</span></p><p class="a">In summer, bands play every night at both ends of the Garden City Pier. Our clients from Virginia describe Virginia Beach as much bigger. One put it this way: nobody here parties like Miami, but people here are enjoying their money.</p></li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">One move we helped with</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A family moved here because their oldest child was starting at Coastal Carolina University. The younger child still needed a school.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The houses they liked sat near the edge of a school zone. The agents checked each address against the district lookup and gave no opinion on any school.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We check the <a href="/buyers/relocating/schools/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">school zone</a> for any address you like, the same way.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="moving-to-myrtle-beach-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Moving to Myrtle Beach FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Myrtle Beach the fastest growing city in America?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No, but it is close. The Myrtle Beach area, which is all of Horry County, grew the second fastest of any metro area from mid-2024 to mid-2025, behind Ocala, Florida. The City of Myrtle Beach itself has about 41,000 people.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are people leaving Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Some are. In the latest count, about 9,100 households left Horry County and about 15,000 arrived. Most who leave go nearby, to Georgetown or Charleston County in South Carolina or Brunswick County, North Carolina.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where do most people moving to Myrtle Beach come from?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About six in seven come from another state, most from the South and the Northeast. The single largest source is Georgetown County, SC. Outside South Carolina, the most come from Suffolk County on Long Island.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is it cheaper to live in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Homes and property tax usually cost less than in the out-of-state counties most movers come from. Home insurance costs more than in the rest of South Carolina, and local pay is lower.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is winter like in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Short and mild. A January day averages a high of about 56 degrees and a low of about 37, and snow averages about an inch a year.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does South Carolina tax Social Security?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No, South Carolina does not tax Social Security. Military retirement pay is not taxed either.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.irs.gov/statistics/soi-tax-stats-migration-data" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS migration</a>, <a href="https://www.census.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026/2025-popest-metro-micro-counties.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census estimates</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT1Y2024.B05002?g=050XX00US45051" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census ACS</a>, <a href="https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/microdata.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ACS microdata</a>, <a href="https://rfa.sc.gov/programs/census-state-liaison-and-data-center/search-and-download-population-data/rfa-population-projections" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC projections</a>, <a href="https://www.bls.gov/cew/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BLS QCEW</a>, <a href="https://www.zillow.com/research/data/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zillow data</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-policies-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenFEMA</a>, <a href="https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/us-climate-normals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA normals</a>, <a href="https://www.weather.gov/ilm/MYRsnowfallDatabase" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NWS snowfall</a>, <a href="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/climo/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA hurricanes</a>, <a href="https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/stationhome.html?id=8661070" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Springmaid Pier</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c006.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-6</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c016.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">12-16</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c037.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">12-37</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t56c003.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">56-3-627</a>. Households: IRS returns that changed county, latest year. Home values: Zillow, by county. Weather: North Myrtle Beach airport normals. Insurance: our count of Census and FEMA data. Listings: counts from the multiple listing service (MLS). Not tax advice.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c