ple, both 66</th><td class="n" data-label="Social Security">$40,000</td><td data-label="Other income">$30,000 private pension</td><td class="n" data-label="State tax">$0</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Single, 67</th><td class="n" data-label="Social Security">$24,000</td><td data-label="Other income">$50,000 New York public pension</td><td class="n" data-label="State tax">about $560</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Couple, 60 and 58</th><td class="n" data-label="Social Security">None</td><td data-label="Other income">$36,000 military retirement pay</td><td class="n" data-label="State tax">$0</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="c3-retcalc c3-calc-box" style="background:var(--navy);background-image:linear-gradient(160deg,rgba(42,48,64,.97),rgba(28,32,40,.98));border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14);border-radius:18px;padding:1.4rem 1.3rem 1.3rem;margin:1.6rem 0;max-width:620px;box-shadow:0 26px 60px -30px rgba(28,32,40,.6)"><p style="font-size:.85rem;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass-2);margin:0 0 .4rem;font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600">Your 2026 South Carolina income tax</p><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.8);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.5;margin:0 0 1rem">Type in your own numbers for one year.</p><div style="display:grid;gap:.7rem"><label class="c3-rl" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.92);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.3"><span>Filing</span><select id="rtJoint" onchange="c3Ret()" style="width:8.2rem;flex:none;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.4);border-radius:8px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;padding:.5rem .6rem;text-align:left"><option value="1" selected>Married</option><option value="0">Single</option></select></label><label class="c3-rl" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.92);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.3"><span>Your age</span><input id="rtAge1" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="0" step="1" value="66" oninput="c3Ret()" style="width:8.2rem;flex:none;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.4);border-radius:8px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;padding:.5rem .6rem;text-align:right"></label><label class="c3-rl" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.92);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.3"><span>Your spouse's age</span><input id="rtAge2" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="0" step="1" value="66" oninput="c3Ret()" style="width:8.2rem;flex:none;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.4);border-radius:8px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;padding:.5rem .6rem;text-align:right"></label><label class="c3-rl" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.92);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.3"><span>Social Security, both of you ($)</span><input id="rtSs" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="0" step="1000" value="40000" oninput="c3Ret()" style="width:8.2rem;flex:none;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.4);border-radius:8px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;padding:.5rem .6rem;text-align:right"></label><label class="c3-rl" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.92);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.3"><span>Your pension, IRA or 401(k) ($)</span><input id="rtRet1" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="0" step="1000" value="30000" oninput="c3Ret()" style="width:8.2rem;flex:none;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.4);border-radius:8px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;padding:.5rem .6rem;text-align:right"></label><label class="c3-rl" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.92);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.3"><span>Your spouse's pension, IRA or 401(k) ($)</span><input id="rtRet2" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="0" step="1000" value="0" oninput="c3Ret()" style="width:8.2rem;flex:none;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.4);border-radius:8px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;padding:.5rem .6rem;text-align:right"></label><label class="c3-rl" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.92);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.3"><span>Military retirement pay ($)</span><input id="rtMil" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="0" step="1000" value="0" oninput="c3Ret()" style="width:8.2rem;flex:none;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.4);border-radius:8px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;padding:.5rem .6rem;text-align:right"></label><label class="c3-rl" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:.8rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.92);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.3"><span>Other income, such as interest or wages ($)</span><input id="rtOther" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="0" step="1000" value="0" oninput="c3Ret()" style="width:8.2rem;flex:none;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.4);border-radius:8px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;padding:.5rem .6rem;text-align:right"></label></div><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline;border-top:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.22);margin-top:1.1rem;padding-top:1rem;font-family:var(--sans);color:rgba(244,239,232,.92)"><span>Estimated state income tax</span><strong id="rtTax" style="color:var(--brass-2);font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.9rem;line-height:1">$0</strong></div><p id="rtSay" aria-live="polite" style="font-family:var(--sans);color:rgba(244,239,232,.85);line-height:1.55;margin:.6rem 0 0;font-size:1rem">Your deductions cover all of your South Carolina income.</p></div><script>/* The 2026 South Carolina income tax estimate, the same rules as data/2026-11-a/buyers-retirees/build_examples.py
