ext":"Yes, through the inlets, most directly Little River Inlet in the north and Murrells Inlet in the south. Check fixed bridge clearances and no-wake stretches on your route, because they decide how long the ride takes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I check before buying a waterfront home?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Water depth at low tide, dock permit status and transferability, bulkhead condition and ownership, the flood zone and real insurance quotes, HOA water rules, and the route to open water. We check all of it as part of the offer work."}}]}</script>
