<span><strong>89%</strong><span class="t">of one South Carolina HOA's court bill was lawyers' fees and court costs</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 7, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">How an association forecloses, how often it happens in Horry County, and the steps that stop it before the sale.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. For a house or a condo, a South Carolina homeowners association (HOA) or <a href="/hoa/hoa-vs-poa/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">condo association</a> can put a lien on your home for unpaid dues and ask a court to sell it. A lien is a legal claim for money owed. The lien is on the home itself, so it applies whether or not you have a mortgage.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The bill that starts it can be small. Lawyers' fees and court costs are added to it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you are sued, you usually have 30 days to answer; the summons, the paper served on you, gives the time. Answer, and get the case itself dismissed, because paying the bill does not by itself end the lawsuit. Or sell before the auction.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Behind on HOA dues? Ask us about selling before the auction.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Talk to an agent</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#can-they-foreclose" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Can they foreclose?</a></li><li><a href="#how-often" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">How often here</a></li><li><a href="#step-by-step" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Step by step</a></li><li><a href="#how-the-bill-grows" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">How the bill grows</a></li><li><a href="#your-mortgage" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Your mortgage</a></li><li><a href="#behind-now" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Behind now</a></li><li><a href="#buying" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Buying</a></li><li><a href="#new-bills" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">New bills</a></li><li><a href="#hoa-liens-and-foreclosure-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">HOA liens and foreclosure FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="can-they-foreclose"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Can they foreclose?">Can an HOA foreclose on your house in South Carolina?</h2><style>main#main .lf-fig{max-width:720px;margin:1.3rem 0 1.5rem;padding:1.1rem 1.2rem 1rem;border-radius:20px;box-sizing:border-box;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(255,255,255,.82),rgba(255,255,255,.58));border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.8);box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.9),0 10px 26px -18px rgba(28,32,40,.35)}main#main .lf-fig .cap{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.0625rem;line-height:1.4;margin:0 0 .8rem}main#main .lf-fig figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.55;margin-top:.8rem}main#main .lf-waffle{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(10,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.4rem;max-width:100%}main#main .lf-waffle li{margin:0;aspect-ratio:1;border-radius:7px;background:#c9c2b6}main#main .lf-waffle li.a{background:#a8482f}main#main .lf-key{list-style:none;margin:.9rem 0 0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:.35rem;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.4;color:var(--navy)}main#main .lf-key li{margin:0;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:.5rem}main#main .lf-key i{flex:0 0 auto;width:1rem;height:1rem;border-radius:4px;margin-top:.2rem;background:#c9c2b6}main#main .lf-key i.a{background:#a8482f}main#main .lf-key b{font-weight:700}main#main .lf-share{position:relative;height:2.6rem;border-radius:999px;background:#c9c2b6;overflow:hidden}main#main .lf-share i{position:absolute;left:0;top:0;bottom:0;background:#a8482f}main#main .lf-share i.lo{width:5%}main#main .lf-shar