run the numbers on a rental</a> shows the math. <a href="/invest/where-to-buy/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Where to buy a rental</a> compares the parts of the Grand Strand by strategy.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Will the rent cover the tax, HOA dues and insurance?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We add its tax, HOA dues and insurance and see if the rent covers them.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us run the numbers</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="best-month"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Best month">When is the best month to rent out a house in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Summer. Asking rents are about half a percent above the year's trend in August, the high, and about 1.4 percent below it in January, the low. A year's lease that starts in summer also ends in summer, so you look for the next tenant in the high months too.</p><figure class="c3-gchart rp-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .8rem">Asking rents each month, above or below the year's trend</span><svg class="rp-n" viewBox="0 0 280 174" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart of asking rents against the year's trend, by month. Rents are above the trend from June to October, highest in August, about half a percent above. They are below it from November to April, lowest in January, about 1.4 percent below."><line x1="42" x2="274" y1="22.4" y2="22.4" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="36" y="27.3" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f