 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/invest/strategies/dscr-loans/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a good DSCR for an investment property?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most lenders want 1.10 to 1.25 or higher on a purchase. That means the rent covers the payment with room to spare. A 1.00 ratio breaks even. Our preferred lender starts writing DSCR loans at a 0.75 ratio. Below 1.00, BrickWood Mortgage still finances the deal, with a larger down payment and a higher rate."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get a DSCR loan in South Carolina with no income verification?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. DSCR loans do not use personal income, tax returns, or debt-to-income ratios. The property's rent and the appraisal carry the application, which is the main reason investors choose them over conventional financing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much down payment does a DSCR loan require?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Expect 15 to 25 percent down on most Grand Strand DSCR loans, from the current BrickWood Mortgage investor programs. Condotels and non-warrantable condos ask for more, and a larger down payment improves both the rate and the qualifying ratio."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use short-term rental income to qualify?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sometimes. Some DSCR lenders accept short-term rental income. Around the Grand Strand, appraisers often provide high short-term rental income estimates, but only 75 percent of that figure can be counted as qualified income, so the number used to qualify is more conservative than the appraisal suggests. Long-term lease income is simpler to qualify on."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a DSCR loan close in an LLC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, and many investors prefer it. Closing in an LLC keeps a portfolio organized and supports partnerships, and a single-owner LLC does not break a 1031 exchange because the tax rules treat you and that LLC as the same taxpayer. Chapter3 coordinates the property and the loan together so the structure is right at closing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get a DSCR loan if the property does not cash flow?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. BrickWood Mortgage writes DSCR loans down to a 0.75 ratio. That suits beach properties you buy for the appreciation, where the rent does not fully cover the payment. Expect a larger down payment and a higher rate. Above 1.00, the program asks for a standard investor down payment."}}]}</script>
