 <p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:760px;margin-bottom:1rem">A DSCR loan qualifies on the property's own rent, not your tax returns. DSCR is short for debt service coverage ratio. It is the rent the home collects, divided by the loan payment it must cover. No W-2s, no tax returns, no debt-to-income math. Most of the Grand Strand investment purchases Chapter3 closes are DSCR loans, so the steps below are the ones our agents and our lending partner run every week.</p><ol style="list-style:none;display:grid;gap:.7rem;margin:1.6rem 0;padding:0;max-width:720px"><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">1</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Find the property.</strong> The loan is judged on the property&#x27;s rent, not on your income.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">2</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">The appraiser sets the market rent.</strong> The lender uses that figure. On a short-term rental, only 75 percent of it counts.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">3</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Divide the rent by the payment.</strong> That figure is the DSCR. Above 1.00 means the rent more than covers the payment.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">4</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Show credit and the down payment.</strong> A score in the high 600s and up, and 15 to 25 percent down on most Grand Strand deals.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">5</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Close in your name or an LLC.</strong> No W-2s and no tax returns are asked for at any step.</p></li></ol>
