-<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/">Invest</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">What is being built</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Permits, hospitals, roads</p><h1 class="detail-h1">What is being built on the Grand Strand right now?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Houses, hospitals and roads.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 9, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Builders were allowed to start 4,978 homes in the Myrtle Beach metro from January through September 2026. One hospital opened. Two more are licensed. The interstate is not being built.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses, mostly. Builders were allowed to start 6,511 homes in the Myrtle Beach metro in 2025, and 4,978 from January to September 2026. That is 3.7 percent below the same months a year earlier.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The county has 44,732 more units already approved and not yet built. Most of them are in Longs, Carolina Forest, Surfside and Burgess.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The big projects are two licensed hospitals, four road jobs under way, and the airport terminal that opened in December 2025. McLeod's new hospital in Carolina Forest is now open. Interstate 73 has right of way and plans. It has no construction contract and no money to build.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The numbers come from the federal permit count and the county's own data. The sections below have each number, its date and where it came from.</p><div style="margin-top:1.4rem"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call a specialized agent</a></div><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:2rem;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#what-is-being-built-in-myrtle-beach-right-now" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What is being built in Myrtle Beach right now?</a></li><li><a href="#how-many-houses-are-being-built" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">How many houses are being built?</a></li><li><a href="#what-is-being-discussed-but-not-yet-approved" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What is being discussed but not yet approved?</a></li><li><a href="#which-hospitals-are-being-built" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which hospitals are being built?</a></li><li><a href="#is-interstate-73-being-built" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Is Interstate 73 being built?</a></li><li><a href="#which-roads-are-under-construction" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which roads are under construction?</a></li><li><a href="#what-else-is-changing-on-the-grand-strand" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What else is changing on the Grand Strand?</a></li><li><a href="#where-can-you-see-the-permits-near-a-house" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where can you see the permits near a house?</a></li><li><a href="#what-does-the-building-mean-for-a-rental-buyer" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What does the building mean for a rental buyer?</a></li><li><a href="#grand-strand-construction-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Grand Strand construction FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-is-being-built-in-myrtle-beach-right-now"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What is being built in Myrtle Beach right now?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The sections below have the detail and the source for each row.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where it stands</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Houses</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">4,978 homes permitted in the metro, January to September 2026; 6,511 in 2025</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Approved and not yet built</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">44,732 units approved through the county's planning office</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Hospitals</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">McLeod Carolina Forest, 48 beds, now open; two more licensed and not yet open, 59 and 36 beds; five free-standing emergency departments</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Interstate 73</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Right of way bought, plans drawn, no construction contract and no construction money</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Roads</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">US 501 to SC 544 and the downtown 501 realignment finishing fall 2026; US 701 north of Conway and the US 17 Bypass six-laning under way</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Airport</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$93.5 million terminal open since December 2025</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Nothing is under construction on Interstate 73. No new bridge to the beach has a contract. The section on roads has what is funded and what is only planned.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="how-many-houses-are-being-built"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">How many houses are being built?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www2.census.gov/econ/bps/CBSA%20(beginning%20Jan%202024)/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The federal government counts the homes that local governments permit each month</a>. The count covers the Myrtle Beach metro, <a href="https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/metro-micro/geographies/reference-files/2023/delineation-files/list1_2023.xlsx" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">which is Horry County</a>. Each month's figure arrives about four weeks after the month ends. The bars show each month's first count. The year totals below are the Census's own, which add late reports and corrections, so the bars do not add up to them exactly.</p><div style="max-width:640px;margin:1rem 0 1.2rem"><svg viewBox="0 0 640 230" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Homes permitted each month in the Myrtle Beach metro, January 2024 to September 2026" style="display:block;max-width:640px;font-family:var(--sans)"><line x1="44" y1="134.66666666666669" x2="630" y2="134.66666666666669" stroke="rgba(28,32,40,.12)"/><text x="39" y="138.66666666666669" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" fill="rgba(28,32,40,.78)">300</text><line x1="44" y1="73.33333333333334" x2="630" y2="73.33333333333334" stroke="rgba(28,32,40,.12)"/><text x="39" y="77.33333333333334" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" fill="rgba(28,32,40,.78)">600</text><line x1="44" y1="12" x2="630" y2="12" stroke="rgba(28,32,40,.12)"/><text x="39" y="16" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" fill="rgba(28,32,40,.78)">900</text><rect x="45.5" y="70.9" width="14.8" height="125.1" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>January 2024: 612 homes</title></rect><text x="46.0" y="218" font-size="11" fill="#1c2028">2024</text><rect x="63.3" y="63.3" width="14.8" height="132.7" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>February 2024: 649 homes</title></rect><rect x="81.0" y="57.2" width="14.8" height="138.8" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>March 2024: 679 homes</title></rect><rect x="98.8" y="59.8" width="14.8" height="136.2" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>April 2024: 666 homes</title></rect><rect x="116.5" y="28.4" width="14.8" height="167.6" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>May 2024: 820 homes</title></rect><rect x="134.3" y="78.6" width="14.8" height="117.4" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>June 2024: 574 homes</title></rect><rect x="152.0" y="73.5" width="14.8" height="122.5" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>July 2024: 599 homes</title></rect><rect x="169.8" y="98.3" width="14.8" height="97.7" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>August 2024: 478 homes</title></rect><rect x="187.6" y="88.7" width="14.8" height="107.3" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>September 2024: 525 homes</title></rect><rect x="205.3" y="75.8" width="14.8" height="120.2" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>October 2024: 588 homes</title></rect><rect x="223.1" y="100.1" width="14.8" height="95.9" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>November 2024: 469 homes</title></rect><rect x="240.8" y="95.2" width="14.8" height="100.8" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>December 2024: 493 homes</title></rect><rect x="258.6" y="73.1" width="14.8" height="122.9" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>January 2025: 601 homes</title></rect><text x="259.1" y="218" font-size="11" fill="#1c2028">2025</text><rect x="276.3" y="72.3" width="14.8" height="123.7" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>February 2025: 605 homes</title></rect><rect x="294.1" y="61.9" width="14.8" height="134.1" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>March 2025: 656 homes</title></rect><rect x="311.9" y="57.8" width="14.8" height="138.2" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>April 2025: 676 homes</title></rect><rect x="329.6" y="56.0" width="14.8" he