"translate(1053.6 622.5)"><circle r="50" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="8"/><text class="pn" y="25" text-anchor="middle">1</text></g><g transform="translate(830.5 679.6)"><circle r="50" fill="#2f6f8f" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="8"/><text class="pn" y="25" text-anchor="middle">2</text></g><g transform="translate(676.3 599.7)"><circle r="50" fill="#5f8a4e" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="8"/><text class="pn" y="25" text-anchor="middle">3</text></g><g transform="translate(616.9 171.3)"><circle r="50" fill="#8a5a9e" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="8"/><text class="pn" y="25" text-anchor="middle">4</text></g><g transform="translate(367.8 1598.8)"><circle r="50" fill="#b3261e" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="8"/><text class="pn" y="25" text-anchor="middle">5</text></g></svg></div><figcaption>The dashed line is the county line. Aerial photo: USGS, public domain. Roads and the county line: U.S. Census Bureau, Horry County and OpenStreetMap contributors.</figcaption><ol class="c3-gc-key" aria-label="The five parts of Garden City"><li><span class="c3-gc-num p1" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span><b style="color:var(--navy)">The ocean side of Waccamaw Drive</b>: the beach and the pier</span></li><li><span class="c3-gc-num p2" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span><b style="color:var(--navy)">On the marsh</b>: docks and tidal creeks</span></li><li><span class="c3-gc-num p3" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span><b style="color:var(--navy)">Between the marsh and Business 17</b>: the most kinds of homes</span></li><li><span class="c3-gc-num p4" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span><b style="color:var(--navy)">West of Business 17</b>: subdivisions lived in all year</span></li><li><span class="c3-gc-num p5" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span><b style="color:var(--navy)">The Georgetown end</b>: canals, docks and the quietest beach</span></li></ol></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="parts"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Five parts">Where to buy in Garden City, SC</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Garden City has five parts, and each is a different way to live at the beach. The numbers match the map above.</p><div class="c3-gc-part" style="--gc-rows:auto auto auto auto 1fr"><h3 id="ocean-side" data-toc="The ocean side of Waccamaw Drive" class="c3-gc-h3"><span class="c3-gc-num p1" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span>The ocean side of Waccamaw Drive: the beach and the pier</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Here you walk out of your building onto the sand. Condo buildings and a few beach houses stand between Waccamaw Drive and the ocean, from the Surfside Beach line south past the pier. The largest buildings include Royal Garden Resort, Waters Edge Resort, Surfmaster and Atalaya Towers.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The pier is the center of this side. At the far end of the Garden City Pier, rebuilt after Hurricane Hugo took the old pier in 1989, the rain shelter holds a bandstand and a dance floor bar, and people learn line dances out over the ocean.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-pier-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-pier-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-pier-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of Garden City Beach, labelled: the Garden City Pier running from the beach into the ocean, buildings and beach houses along Waccamaw Drive, and Atlantic Avenue crossing the salt marsh" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The ocean side by the pier from above: buildings and beach houses between Waccamaw Drive and the beach, and the salt marsh behind.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Its café serves breakfast. In summer, its deck bar has karaoke in the afternoons, and bands play every night at both ends of the pier, weather permitting. The arcade is there for a rainy day. A pier pass covers fishing, so no state fishing license is needed, and in summer you can fish around the clock.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Almost every home on this side is a condo. Condos here sold for about $320,000 at the middle in the past year.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="gc-ocean-side" data-name="Garden City by the pier" data-head="Condos for sale by the Garden City Pier now"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Garden%20City's%20ocean%20side">Get the condos for sale on Garden City's ocean side<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="c3-gc-part" style="--gc-rows:auto auto auto 1fr"><h3 id="on-the-marsh" data-toc="On the marsh" class="c3-gc-h3"><span class="c3-gc-num p2" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span>On the marsh: docks and tidal creeks</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Behind the beach strip is salt marsh, cut by tidal creeks that reach the inlet at Garden City Point. The houses along its edges look out over the marsh, and many have <a href="/buyers/waterfront-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">a long private dock</a>. On the beach strip they line Dogwood Drive. On the mainland side they are on streets like Creekside Drive and Rum Gully Road.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From a dock on the marsh, you can tie a chicken neck to a string and pull up blue crabs for dinner. In South Carolina you need no license to crab with three or fewer drop nets, fold-up traps or hand lines.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Beach houses in rows between the ocean beach and a wide marsh with tidal creeks and boat docks at Garden City Beach, seen from a plane over the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Beach houses along Waccamaw Drive, seen from over the ocean, with the salt marsh and its creeks behind them and docks on the far shore.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">These are the most costly houses east of Business 17. The ones that sold in the past year went for about $1.24 million at the middle, about twice the other houses east of Business 17. Few come up for sale.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="gc-on-the-marsh" data-name="Garden City on the marsh" data-head="Houses for sale around the Garden City marsh now"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Garden%20City">Get the marsh-front homes for sale in Garden City<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="c3-gc-part" style="--gc-rows:auto auto auto 1fr"><h3 id="older-streets" data-toc="Between the marsh and Business 17" class="c3-gc-h3"><span class="c3-gc-num p3" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span>Between the marsh and Business 17: the most kinds of homes</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The rest of the land between the marsh and Business 17 is streets of houses, small condo buildings and manufactured homes. Its neighborhoods include Salters Cove, Mount Gilead, Myrtle Dunes and Woodland Terrace. It also takes in the streets north of where Waccamaw Drive ends, up to the Surfside Beach line.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every Fourth of July afternoon, Garden City holds a "wet" golf cart parade: decorated carts drive the route while people on the side soak them with water guns. It raises money for local first responders.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-streets-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-streets-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-streets-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of streets of houses under trees in Garden City, with a pond at the top and the salt marsh at the lower right, labelled" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Streets between the marsh and Business 17 from above: houses and yards, a pond, and the salt marsh at the lower right.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This part has the widest range of prices. Away from the marsh, a house sold for about $575,000 at the middle in the past year. Condos and manufactured homes cost less. Where a home is on rented land, the lot rent is not in the price, and we find it out for each home.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="gc-older-streets" data-name="Garden City between the marsh and Business 17" data-head="Homes for sale between the marsh and Business 17 now"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Garden%20City%20east%20of%20Business%2017">Get the homes for sale in Garden City east of Business 17<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="c3-gc-part" style="--gc-rows:auto auto auto 1fr"><h3 id="west-of-17" data-toc="West of Business 17" class="c3-gc-h3"><span class="c3-gc-num p4" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span>West of Business 17: subdivisions lived in all year</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">West of Business 17 are Garden City's subdivisions, with houses on curving streets around ponds. The largest are Woodlake Village, Mallard Landing, Harbour Village and Jamestowne. Condo communities include Sweetwater at Indian Wells, South Bay Lakes, Southbridge and Tupelo Bay Golf Villas.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the Fourth of July, decorated boats parade along the inlet in the afternoon while the crowd watches from the MarshWalk, and fireworks go up at night. In 2025 the boat parade was at 2 p.m. and the fireworks at 10 p.m. From the subdivisions west of Business 17, it is a short drive.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-west-of-17-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-west-of-17-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-west-of-17-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of subdivisions west of Business 17 in Garden City: houses on curving streets around ponds, a swimming pool and sports courts, with woods at the upper right" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Subdivisions west of Business 17 from above: houses on curving streets, ponds, a pool and courts, and woods.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">More people live here all year: about 3 in 4 houses are taxed as the owner's main home, the most of any part. A house sold for about $340,000 at the middle in the past year and a condo for about $173,000, the lowest prices in Garden City.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="gc-west-of-17" data-name="Garden City west of Business 17" data-head="Homes for sale west of Business 17 now"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Garden%20City%20west%20of%20Business%2017">Get the homes for sale in Garden City west of Business 17<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="c3-gc-part" style="--gc-rows:auto auto auto auto 1fr"><h3 id="georgetown-end" data-toc="The Georgetown end" class="c3-gc-h3"><span class="c3-gc-num p5" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span>The Georgetown end: canals, docks and the quietest beach</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South of the county line, Waccamaw Drive runs on to Garden City Point, where the marsh meets the inlet. Houses line the beach, and behind them many sit on canals with private docks.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At the inlet end of Waccamaw Drive, Gulfstream Cafe has looked over Murrells Inlet for nearly 40 years. People go up to its rooftop deck to watch the sun set over the water, and come back for its oyster roasts in season.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-point-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-point-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-point-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of the south end of Garden City Beach, labelled: houses on curving canals with private docks between the inlet water at left and Waccamaw Drive and the Atlantic Ocean at right" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The Georgetown end near Garden City Point from above: houses on canals with private docks, Waccamaw Drive and the beach.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This is the quietest stretch of the beach road. Georgetown County's rules apply here. It requires no business license for a rental, and its lodging tax is lower.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Prices here are the highest in Garden City. The listings here asked about $1.45 million at the middle, more than any other part.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="gc-georgetown-end" data-name="the Georgetown end of Garden City" data-head="Homes for sale at the Georgetown end now"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Garden%20City's%20Georgetown%20end">Get the homes for sale at Garden City's Georgetown end<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Home prices">What do homes in Garden City cost?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The chart gives the middle sale price in each part over the past year, from Horry County's deed records. Houses cost the most on the marsh and the least west of Business 17.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="The lowest prices are west of Business 17"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">The lowest prices are west of Business 17</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Part and kind of home</span><span role="columnheader">Middle price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">A house on the marsh</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,240,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">A house between the marsh and 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.465" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$575,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">A house west of Business 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.275" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$340,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">A condo on the ocean side</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.259" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$320,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">A condo west of Business 17</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.139" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$173,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Middle sale price in the past year, from Horry County's deed records, so the Georgetown end is not in it.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Asking prices are usually higher than sale prices.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Know what the Garden City home you like is worth</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We pull the recent sales in its building or on its street, and tell you what those sales say it is worth.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us pull the sales for one home</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="airbnb"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting it out">Can you Airbnb in Garden City, SC?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, unless the building's own rules say no. There is no town, so no town rental ordinance applies. Horry County's list of what a nightly-rental owner must file names a business license and three tax accounts, and no rental permit. We go over the filings with you before you close.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condo association or an HOA (homeowners association) can forbid or limit rentals in its own papers. We read the building's documents and rules before you offer. Our page on <a href="/hoa/rental-restrictions/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">HOA rental restrictions</a> explains how those rules work.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Guests pay lodging taxes on top of the rent: about 12 percent on the Horry side and about 11 percent on the Georgetown end. You collect that money and send it on, so it is not part of your income.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What a Garden City Airbnb earns</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">AirROI, a rental data company, tracks the Airbnb listings here under the name Garden City Beach. Over the past 12 months:</p><ul class="c3-gc-stats" aria-label="Airbnb numbers for Garden City Beach, past 12 months"><li><b>$41,200</b><span>the average listing's income in a year</span></li><li><b>40%</b><span>of nights booked</span></li><li><b>$371</b><span>average nightly rate</span></li><li><b>374</b><span>active listings</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each figure is an average across all the listings, so the nights booked times the nightly rate does not come out to the income.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of the money comes in summer. A listing earns about 5 times as much in an average July as in January.</p><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gc-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .5rem">Summer pays: a July earns about 5 times a January</span><svg class="c3-gc-cols" viewBox="0 0 360 236" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Column chart of what a Garden City Beach Airbnb earns in an average month: January $2,090, February $2,820, March $3,660, April $4,390, May $5,660, June $8,690, July $10,200, August $6,540, September $4,120, October $3,490, November $2,740, December $2,670."><line x1="76" x2="352" y1="200" y2="200" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="70" y="205" text-anchor="end">$0</text><line x1="76" x2="352" y1="120.9" y2="120.9" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".12"/><text x="70" y="125.9" text-anchor="end">$5,000</text><line x1="76" x2="352" y1="41.8" y2="41.8" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".12"/><text x="70" y="46.8" text-anchor="end">$10,000</text><rect x="79.2" y="166.9" width="16.6" height="33.1" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="87.5" y="222" text-anchor="middle">J</text><text class="v" x="87.5" y="147.4" text-anchor="middle">$2,090</text><rect x="102.2" y="155.4" width="16.6" height="44.6" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="110.5" y="222" text-anchor="middle">F</text><rect x="125.2" y="142.1" width="16.6" height="57.9" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="133.5" y="222" text-anchor="middle">M</text><rect x="148.2" y="130.6" width="16.6" height="69.4" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="156.5" y="222" text-anchor="middle">A</text><rect x="171.2" y="110.5" width="16.6" height="89.5" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="179.5" y="222" text-anchor="middle">M</text><rect x="194.2" y="62.5" width="16.6" height="137.5" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="202.5" y="222" text-anchor="middle">J</text><rect x="217.2" y="38.7" width="16.6" height="161.3" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="225.5" y="222" text-anchor="middle">J</text><text class="v" x="225.5" y="30.7" text-anchor="middle">$10,200</text><rect x="240.2" y="96.5" width="16.6" height="103.5" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="248.5" y="222" text-anchor="middle">A</text><rect x="263.2" y="134.8" width="16.6" height="65.2" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="271.5" y="222" text-anchor="middle">S</text><rect x="286.2" y="144.8" width="16.6" height="55.2" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="294.5" y="222" text-anchor="middle">O</text><rect x="309.2" y="156.7" width="16.6" height="43.3" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="317.5" y="222" text-anchor="middle">N</text><rect x="332.2" y="157.8" width="16.6" height="42.2" rx="3" fill="#d9b48f"/><text x="340.5" y="222" text-anchor="middle">D</text></svg><figcaption>What one Airbnb listing here earned in an average month, from AirROI, before cleaning, fees and management. Darker columns are May to August.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Worked example: an ocean-side condo, rented by the night</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Take the middle ocean-side condo from part 1, and say it earns what the average listing here earns. No loan is in this example.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">One year of nightly renting</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">About</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Airbnb income, the average listing's year, before fees</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$41,200</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Less the property tax as a rental, with the county fees on the bill</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$4,070</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Less your own flood policy on the unit</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,560</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Less condo dues, at the middle of 35 ocean-side listings (about $790 a month)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$9,480</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Left for cleaning, management, utilities and the unit's other insurance</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$26,100</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The dues are what the listing agents report. For the middle half of these condos they run from about $610 to $910 a month. The building's own flood policy is paid out of them.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not in the table:</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">Cleaning and management, which depend on who you hire.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">Utilities, and the unit's insurance other than flood.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">A special assessment, if the building charges one on top of the dues.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We get the unit's own dues, the building's budget and an insurance quote for the unit before you offer, so you see the whole year before you buy.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Thinking of renting a Garden City condo by the night?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the building or the address. We read its condo papers on renting, and we price the dues, the tax and the flood policy for that unit.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask about a Garden City condo</a></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">AirROI's figures cover every kind of home here, condos and houses together. To see what a nightly rental earns in other towns, <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">compare all nine submarkets</a>. The rules by town are on our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="things-to-do"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Things to do">What is there to do in Garden City, SC?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A summer day here starts on the beach and ends on the pier. For dinner, the <a href="https://marshwalk.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MarshWalk</a> in Murrells Inlet is about 8 minutes away by car. The <a href="/submarkets/murrells-inlet/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Murrells Inlet guide</a> has its restaurants and the boat landing at its south end.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a day out, <a href="https://southcarolinaparks.com/huntington-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Huntington Beach State Park</a> is 15 to 20 minutes south. It has 3 miles of beach, a freshwater lake where you are almost sure to see alligators, and what the state calls some of the top bird-watching on the East Coast. The <a href="/submarkets/pawleys-island/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Pawleys Island guide</a> has the park's history and Brookgreen Gardens across the road.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For groceries, Kroger on Business 17 is about 4 minutes from the pier by car, and the Walmart Supercenter on the Garden City Connector about 5.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The beach rules</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County manages the beach from the Surfside Beach town line to the Georgetown County line. Its rules:</p><ul class="c3-gc-rules"><li><strong>Dogs</strong>Off the beach from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m., May 1 through Labor Day. Otherwise on a hand-held leash.</li><li><strong>Shade</strong>Round umbrellas up to 7 feet 6 inches across, and small pop-up cabanas for infants. No tents or canopies, all year.</li><li><strong>Overnight</strong>Nothing may be left on the beach overnight.</li><li><strong>Alcohol</strong>None on the beach or the beach accesses.</li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is everything?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Drive times by car from the foot of the pier, without traffic. Summer traffic on Business 17 and US 17 adds time.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">From the Garden City Pier to</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">By car, about</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Surfside Beach pier</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">8 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Market Common</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach International Airport</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Coastal Grand Mall</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Broadway at the Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">25 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Grand Strand Medical Center</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">30 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="winter"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Winter">Is Garden City, SC busy in winter?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Summer is busy and winter is quiet, most of all on the beach road.</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">On the ocean side, more than 9 in 10 homes are second homes or rentals. The county mails most of their tax bills to another state, North Carolina, New York, Pennsylvania and Ohio most often.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">At the last Census, taken in April, about 4 in 5 homes along Waccamaw Drive had no one living in them.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The pier stays open in winter, with shorter hours for fishing and the deck bar.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">From November 1 to February 28, you may drive a golf cart onto the Horry County beach, with a state permit and a licensed driver.</li></ul><div class="c3-gc-story"><b>Example.</b> In the winter cart season, a golf cart with a cooler and buckets drives down onto the sand at Garden City. The beach is empty. There is time for sandcastles, lunch and an hour of watching the waves.</div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="flooding"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flooding">Does Garden City flood?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">East of Business 17, much of Garden City is in FEMA's high-risk flood zone. In that zone a lender requires flood insurance:</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Part of Garden City, Horry side</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Homes in FEMA's high-risk flood zone</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The ocean side of Waccamaw Drive</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Nearly all</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Between the marsh and Business 17</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About half</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">West of Business 17</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">None</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Flood insurance costs about five times as much on the beach strip. Along Waccamaw Drive, the middle federal flood policy on a house cost about $3,260 a year. Elsewhere in Garden City's ZIP code it was about $620.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condo building's own flood policy on the strip cost about $17,000 a year at the middle, shared by the owners through their dues.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What the big storms did</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In September 1989, Hurricane Hugo's storm surge wiped out up to 90 percent of Garden City's homes. The pier was destroyed, and sand covered roads three blocks inland.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In 2022, Hurricane Ian's surge broke through the dunes in Garden City Beach and flooded parking lots and streets. It left up to three feet of sand on South Waccamaw Drive.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">High tides are rising</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">High tides that reach flood level come more often than they used to. At the nearest working tide gauge, in Myrtle Beach, they came about 8 days a year in the last ten years, against 1 or 2 days a year twenty years before.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="High tides reach flood level about 8 days a year now, up from 2"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">High tides reach flood level about 8 days a year now, up from 2</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Years</span><span role="columnheader">Days a year</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1995 to 2004</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.133" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 2 days</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2005 to 2014</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.267" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 3 days</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2015 to 2024</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.7" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 8 days</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">NOAA's outlook for the coming year</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">8 to 12 days</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Days a year, the average for each ten years, at NOAA's tide gauge at Springmaid Pier in Myrtle Beach, about 7 miles north.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our pages on <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">finding out whether a house has flooded</a> and <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance</a> show what we look at.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the flood zone and flood history of one Garden City home</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We pull its flood zone, look for past flooding and, for a condo, get the building's flood policy.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us check a home for flooding</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does it cost to own a home in Garden City each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina figures property tax on a share of a home's value: 4 percent of it for the home you live in, and 6 percent for a second home or rental. The home you live in also skips the school operating tax. As a rental, the same condo pays about 3 times the tax it pays as your main home.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For the middle ocean-side condo:</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Each year</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Your main home</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Second home or rental</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Property tax</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,260</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$3,980</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">County fees on the tax bill</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$89.40</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$89.40</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Your own flood policy on the unit, if you buy one</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,560</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,560</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Condo dues, at the middle of the listings</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$9,480</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$9,480</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The flood policy line is the middle federal policy that condo owners along Waccamaw Drive bought for their own unit. The building's own policy is in the condo dues.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">On the Georgetown end, Georgetown County decides the tax rate. The same state rule applies.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax calculator</a> has the rate for every part of the county.</li></ul><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the yearly cost of one Garden City address</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We work out its tax at the 4 percent rate for a home you live in and at the 6 percent rate for a rental. We show you how to apply for the lower one.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us work out the tax on an address</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="nearby"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Nearby towns">Garden City, Surfside Beach or Murrells Inlet?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The three places sit side by side, and each suits a different buyer.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Place</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Who makes the local rules</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Vacation homes, whole Census place</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Garden City</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The county</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 4 in 10</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/submarkets/surfside-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Surfside Beach</a></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Its own town council</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 4 in 10</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/submarkets/murrells-inlet/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Murrells Inlet</a></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The county</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 1 in 7</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Vacation-use shares are from the 2020 Census. Garden City's share counts the subdivisions west of Business 17 too, so it is lower than along the beach road. Surfside Beach's pier is about 6 minutes north of the Garden City Pier by car, and the MarshWalk about 8 minutes south.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Surfside Beach is a town, so its own rules on renting apply on top of the county's. Murrells Inlet is lived in all year far more than the two beach places, and the MarshWalk's restaurants are there. Garden City has the pier, the marsh and the Georgetown end's canals.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="garden-city-sc-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Garden City, SC FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Garden City, SC in Horry County or Georgetown County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Both. The pier is in Horry County, and most of the beach road is in Georgetown County.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Garden City part of Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Garden City is not part of any city. Most addresses use Murrells Inlet, ZIP code 29576.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you drive a golf cart on Garden City Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the Horry County beach, from November 1 to February 28, with a state permit and a licensed driver.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are dogs allowed on Garden City Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m., May 1 through Labor Day, on the Horry County beach. At other times, on a hand-held leash no longer than 7 feet.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Garden City, SC safe?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. On the Horry side, the Horry County Police Department, the county's main law enforcement agency, answers calls. On the Georgetown end, the Georgetown County Sheriff's Office does.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What schools serve Garden City, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Schools are assigned by address. Homes on the Horry side are in Horry County Schools, and homes on the Georgetown end are in the Georgetown County School District. We look up the assigned schools for any home you like.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county deeds</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table?g=160XX00US4528455" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census 2020</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/monjnvh0/sales-tax-chart-short-term-rentals.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county STR filings</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/tax/accommodations" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR</a>, <a href="https://www.gtcountysc.gov/351/Hospitality-Accommodations-Tax" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown County</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/garden-city-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AirROI</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-policies-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenFEMA policies</a>, <a href="https://www.weather.gov/ilm/hurricanehugo" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NWS Hugo</a>, <a href="https://www.weather.gov/ilm/hurricaneian" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NWS Ian</a>, <a href="https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/stationhome.html?id=8661070" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Springmaid Pier</a>, <a href="https://horrycountysc.gov/about-our-beaches" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county beach rules</a>, <a href="https://www.gardencitypier.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the pier</a>, <a href="https://www.pieratgardencity.com/story" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">pier history</a>, <a href="https://www.dnr.sc.gov/fish/swfaqs.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDNR</a>, <a href="https://www.myrtlebeachareacvb.com/news/myrtle-beach-lights-up-july-4th-with-fireworks-festivals-and-family-fun" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">July 4th</a>, <a href="https://gulfstreamcafe.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gulfstream Cafe</a>, <a href="https://marshwalk.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the MarshWalk</a>, <a href="https://southcarolinaparks.com/huntington-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC State Parks</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/police/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County Police</a>, <a href="https://www.gcsheriff.org/enforcement-division/patrol/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown Sheriff</a>. Our counts: county parcels, flood maps, the past year's deeds; CCMLS listings in aggregate; drives from the pier.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">The ocean side by the pier from above: buildings and beach houses between Waccamaw Drive and the beach, and the salt marsh behind. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service and added labels placed from map data.</div><div role="listitem">Beach houses along Waccamaw Drive, seen from over the ocean, with the salt marsh and its creeks behind them and docks on the far shore. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Streets between the marsh and Business 17 from above: houses and yards, a pond, and the salt marsh at the lower right. Photo