oke-linejoin:round;">N</text><line x1="1416" y1="2281" x2="2221" y2="2281" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="18"/><text x="1819" y="2211" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:105px;font-weight:600;fill:#2f6276;font-style:italic;">half a mile</text></svg></div><p class="c3-sb-panel">North of the pier</p><div class="c3-sb-frame"><svg class="c3-sb-map" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="1581 0 2556 2371" role="img" aria-labelledby="c3-sb-map-n"><title id="c3-sb-map-n">The north half of the town, from the pier to the north town line. Map of the Town of Surfside Beach, turned so the beach runs along the bottom. An orange band along the ocean marks the blocks where nightly rentals are allowed. A larger green area inland marks the streets where rentals under 30 days are not allowed. Gray areas are other districts. North of the pier the line between them follows Dogwood Drive North; south of the pier it follows Willow Drive South, then Lakeside Drive. US 17 Business runs along the inland edge. Ocean Lakes Family Campground, outside the town, is at the north end.</title><use href="#c3-sb-mapg"/><text x="1901" y="2083" text-anchor="end" style="font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:135px;font-weight:700;fill:#1c2028;paint-order:stroke;stroke:#fff;stroke-width:24px;stroke-linejoin:round;">Pier</text><text x="2573" y="599" text-anchor="middle" style="font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:125px;font-weight:700;fill:#1c2028;paint-order:stroke;stroke:#fff;stroke-width:24px;stroke-linejoin:round;">US 17 Business</text><text x="3707" y="1124" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(-76.0 3707 1124)" style="font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:100px;font-weight:600;fill:#2a3040;paint-order:stroke;stroke:#fff;stroke-width:24px;stroke-linejoin:round;">16th Ave N</text><text x="2878" y="1421" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(-77.5 2878 1421)" style="font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,sans-se