+			<td colspan="5" style="border-bottom: 1px solid !important;">your gain that is eligible for exclusion from your income is not to be reported on your tax return. The <a class="xmlbc-link" href="#en_US_2025_publink100011873" id="en_US_2025_publink1000139774" title="Reporting Your Home Sale"><span class="emphasis"><em>Reporting Your Home Sale</em></span></a> section only applies to your nonqualified use gain. However, you may need to complete Form 8949 if Form 1099-S was received. See <a class="xmlbc-link" href="#en_US_2025_publink100011875" id="en_US_2025_publink1000143173" title="Reporting Gain or Loss on Your Home Sale"><span class="emphasis"><em>Reporting Gain or Loss on Your Home Sale</em></span></a>, later.</td>
