 house is taxed around $1,300 a year</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;padding:.55rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;flex:none">+</span><span>Sunnier than the northern cities most people leave</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;padding:.55rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;flex:none">+</span><span>Traffic is light compared with any large metro</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;padding:.55rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;flex:none">+</span><span>Golf carts are a real way to get around in many neighborhoods</span></div></div><div style="background:var(--ivory);padding:1.3rem 1.4rem"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .7rem">Cons of living in Myrtle Beach</h3><div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;padding:.55rem 0;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--slate);font-weight:600;flex:none">&minus;</span><span>You cannot walk to much. This is a driving area</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;padding:.55rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--slate);font-weight:600;flex:none">&minus;</span><span>Pay is lower than in a northern metro</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;padding:.55rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--slate);font-weight:600;flex:none">&minus;</span><span>Summers are hot and humid, with about 22 days a year over 90 degrees</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;padding:.55rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--slate);font-weight:600;flex:none">&minus;</span><span>Hurricane season runs June to November</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;padding:.55rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--slate);font-weight:600;flex:none">&minus;</span><span>Insurance costs more on the oceanfront, though it drops inland</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;padding:.55rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--slate);font-weight:600;flex:none">&minus;</span><span>Your car is taxed every year, which is new for most movers</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;padding:.55rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--slate);font-weight:600;flex:none">&minus;</span><span>More mosquitoes than a dense city</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;padding:.55rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55"><span aria-hidden="true" style="color:var(--slate);font-weight:600;flex:none">&minus;</span><span>Some specialist medical care means a drive to Charleston</span></div></div></div><div style="${S.ctaBox}"><p style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;font-weight:600">Want to see what your budget buys here before you decide?</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass" href="#lead-form">Show me homes</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div>
 </div></section>
 
-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">Money</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">What it costs to live in Myrtle Beach</h2><p style="${S.p}">Housing is where you gain. A typical home here costs about $342,000. The same measure is about $737,000 in the New York area, $742,000 in Boston and $580,000 in Washington. Rent is about 17 percent below the national average.</p><p style="${S.p}">Everything else is closer to normal. Food, power and everyday items sit near the national average, so do not plan on the grocery bill falling. Pay is lower here too, which matters if you are still working.</p><p style="${S.pLast}">Two costs are new. South Carolina taxes your car every year, which most northern states do not, and a second home is taxed at about three times the rate of a main home. Both are covered on our ${A('/buyers/relocating/cost-of-living/', 'cost of living page')}, which compares your city with this one directly.</p></div></section>
+<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">Money</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">What it costs to live in Myrtle Beach</h2><p style="${S.p}">Housing is where you gain. A typical home here costs about $342,000. The same measure is about $737,000 in the New York area, $742,000 in Boston and $580,000 in Washington. Rent is about 17 percent below the national average.</p><p style="${S.p}">Everything else is closer to normal. Food, power and everyday items sit near the national average, so do not plan on the grocery bill falling. ${A('/buyers/relocating/jobs/', 'Pay is lower here too')}, which matters if you are still working.</p><p style="${S.pLast}">Two costs are new. South Carolina taxes your car every year, which most northern states do not, and a second home is taxed at about three times the rate of a main home. Both are covered on our ${A('/buyers/relocating/cost-of-living/', 'cost of living page')}, which compares your city with this one directly.</p></div></section>
 
 <section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">Weather</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">What the weather is like</h2><h3 style="${S.h3}">Winters are mild</h3><p style="${S.p}">January averages a high near 56 and a low in the mid 30s. Snow is rare: about an inch a year on average, and most years get none. Two recent winters each produced a 5 inch storm, and the record is 14 inches from a Christmas storm in 1989. When it does snow, roads and schools close for a day or two, because there is no reason to own plows here.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">Summers are hot and humid</h3><p style="${S.p}">July averages a high near 87 and a low near 72. The area gets about 22 days a year at or above 90 degrees and almost none at 100, so the raw temperature is not extreme. The humidity is what people feel. Most newcomers say they adjust within a season or two.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">It is brighter than most places people leave</h3><p style="${S.pLast}">The nearest long term weather station records about 62 percent of possible sunshine and 111 clear days a year. Pittsburgh averages about 42 percent, Buffalo about 47 percent, and Cleveland about 66 clear days. People from those cities notice it in the first month. The month by month numbers, including ocean water temperatures, are on our ${A('/buyers/relocating/weather/', 'weather page')}.</p></div></section>
 
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@ const spec = {
 
 <section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">If you run a business</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">You cannot charge northern prices here</h2><p style="${S.pLast}">Business owners who move down repeatedly find they have to cut their rates. That is not a local quirk, it is the same fact that made the housing cheap: prices and wages across this market are lower than in a northern metro, so the going rate for your work is lower too. If your plan depends on keeping your old prices, price your service against local competitors before you count on the income. Plenty of people make the trade happily, because the lower cost of living absorbs it. It is only a problem when nobody warned you.</p></div></section>
 
-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">Healthcare</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">What medical care is here, and what is a drive</h2><p style="${S.p}">Better covered than most areas this size, and expanding. Grand Strand Medical Center in Myrtle Beach has 403 beds and is a verified adult Level I trauma center, so the most serious adult emergencies are treated here rather than transferred. Conway Medical Center has 222 beds, McLeod Health Seacoast in Little River 155, Tidelands Waccamaw in Murrells Inlet 124, Tidelands Georgetown 131 and McLeod Health Loris 50.</p><p style="${S.p}">McLeod held a ribbon cutting for its new 48-bed hospital in Carolina Forest in August 2026. Two more hospitals are under construction. One is a 59-bed Grand Strand Health hospital on the US-17 Bypass, expected in late 2027. The other is a 36-bed Tidelands hospital with MUSC at the SC-31 and SC-707 interchange, expected in late 2028. Bed counts and timelines come from each health system.</p><p style="${S.pLast}">What is not here is Level I pediatric trauma and organ transplant. Both are at MUSC in Charleston, about two hours south, and some specialist care follows the same pattern. For veterans, the Myrtle Beach VA clinic is outpatient only and the nearest VA medical center is also in Charleston.</p></div></section>
+<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">Healthcare</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">What medical care is here, and what is a drive</h2><p style="${S.p}">Better covered than most areas this size, and expanding. Grand Strand Medical Center in Myrtle Beach has 403 beds and is a verified adult Level I trauma center, so the most serious adult emergencies are treated here rather than transferred. Conway Medical Center has 222 beds, McLeod Health Seacoast in Little River 155, Tidelands Waccamaw in Murrells Inlet 124, Tidelands Georgetown 131 and McLeod Health Loris 50.</p><p style="${S.p}">McLeod held a ribbon cutting for its new 48-bed hospital in Carolina Forest in August 2026. ${A('/buyers/relocating/healthcare/', 'Two more hospitals are under construction')}. One is a 59-bed Grand Strand Health hospital on the US-17 Bypass, expected in late 2027. The other is a 36-bed Tidelands hospital with MUSC at the SC-31 and SC-707 interchange, expected in late 2028. Bed counts and timelines come from each health system.</p><p style="${S.pLast}">What is not here is Level I pediatric trauma and organ transplant. Both are at MUSC in Charleston, about two hours south, and some specialist care follows the same pattern. For veterans, the Myrtle Beach VA clinic is outpatient only and the nearest VA medical center is also in Charleston.</p></div></section>
 
 <section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">Small stuff that is not small</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">Bugs, and the rest of coastal life</h2><p style="${S.pLast}">Mosquitoes are more noticeable than in a dense city, because much of the county is low, wet and rural. Horry County runs a mosquito control program with truck and aerial spraying that starts in early May, and residents outside city limits can request treatment. Near marsh you also meet biting midges, which everyone here calls no-see-ums. They are small enough to pass through a standard screen, so a finer mesh and a fan on the porch do more than repellent. The big outdoor bugs locals call palmetto bugs live in trees and mulch, not inside houses, and one wanders indoors now and then. None of this is a reason not to move. All of it is a reason to budget for pest control and look at the screens.</p></div></section>
 
